data/raw/*
# Track the scraper outputs themselves so production refreshes commit
# them back to the repo and a fresh checkout has data to work with
# (changed 2026-06-21 — previously gitignored entirely, which meant the
# local CSV could silently lag production by months because nothing
# ever pulled it down).
# 2026-09-26: the full Kalshi/Polymarket scrapes (~63 MB per run) are no
# longer committed (repo pack had reached 666 MB; GitHub rejects files
# >100 MB). The full refresh commits data/reprice/ instead: just the rows
# the 2-hourly re-price needs (scripts/trim_reprice_inputs.py).
!data/raw/predictit_markets.csv
!data/raw/orderbook_depth.csv
data/processed/*
# But DO track the human-maintained exclude list
!data/processed/excluded_pairs.json
# And the incumbents JSON — slowly-changing, read by utils/races.py at
# import time, useful to have committed so a fresh checkout has it
# before the house_incumbents scraper runs.
!data/processed/house_incumbents.json
# And the election_pairs CSV — produced by scripts/elections.py, fed
# into arb_scanner. Useful to inspect committed.
!data/processed/election_pairs.csv
!data/processed/series_review.csv
!data/processed/matched_pairs.csv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
